# SafeMining VR HUD and UI

## Brand colors

| Token | Hex | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| Primary | `#1A365D` | HUD backgrounds, headers |
| Secondary | `#F97316` | CTAs, active progress |
| Tertiary | `#334155` | Borders, secondary text |
| Neutral | `#F9FAFB` | Text on dark panels |
| Success | `#22C55E` | Objective achieved |
| Error | `#EF4444` | Failures, alerts |

Use `Brand.PrimaryColor`, `Brand.SecondaryColor` from BrandConfig when applying at runtime.

## World-space canvas (Quest 3S)

- Distance: 1.5–2m from player
- Scale: ~0.001 on canvas transform
- Minimum touch target: 48×48 px equivalent
- Minimum body text: ~24pt TMP at default scale
- Contrast ratio ≥ 4.5:1 for text on panels

## HUD layout (target Slice 1)

- Top-left: active objective + checklist (5 objectives)
- Top-right: session timer + scenario indicator (1/3, 2/3, 3/3)
- Bottom: subtitles / briefing (`TranslatableText`)
- Menu button with confirmation dialog

## Comfort

- Prefer teleport over smooth locomotion
- Avoid full-screen flashing on errors
- Panel follow: use `Util_PanelFollower` pattern from XR Standard Menu
- Billboarding: subtle, not every frame if performance-critical

## ALWAYS

1. Bind text via `TranslatableText` + `translationID` in es.xml/en.xml
2. Reuse sprites from `Assets/SafeMining/Shared/UI/` when available
3. Test UI at Quest resolution (1832×1920 per eye approximate)

## NEVER

1. Use screen-space overlay canvas for in-simulation HUD
2. Hardcode Spanish strings in simulation scripts
3. Use motion-heavy animations on persistent HUD elements
